hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18922","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Shuayb informed us, from al-Zuhri, Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, that Abdullah ibn Adi ibn al-Hamra al-Zuhri informed him that he heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while standing at al-Hazwarah in the market of Makkah: By Allah, you are the best land of Allah and the most beloved land of Allah to Allah, mighty and majestic, and were I not expelled from you, I would not have left."
"18923","Yaqub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Salih, he said: Ibn Shihab said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Abdullah ibn Adi ibn al-Hamra informed him that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while standing at al-Hazwarah of Makkah, saying to Makkah: By Allah, you are the best land of Allah and the most beloved land of Allah to Allah, mighty and majestic, and were I not expelled from you, I would not have left."
"18924","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood at al-Hazwarah and said: I knew that you are the best land of Allah and the most beloved land to Allah, and were your people not to have expelled me from you, I would not have left. Abd al-Razzaq said: Al-Hazwarah is at the gate of the grain sellers."
"18925","Ibrahim ibn Khalid narrated to us, Rabah narrated to us, from Mamar, from Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from some of them, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, while in the market of al-Hazwarah: By Allah, you are the best land of Allah and the most beloved land to Allah, and were I not expelled from you, I would not have left."
